  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "_comment": "NPCI UPI deeplink `purpose` codes (plus the `mode` codes that carry a cap or recurring meaning). Everything the app derives from a purpose code lives here, so it can be corrected via the remote catalog sync without an app update. `category` is OPTIONAL and appears only on codes that genuinely imply a spend category — a code without it never contributes an auto-category. Category names MUST match the vocabulary in mcc.json, otherwise the two sources fragment into near-duplicate buckets. `capInr` is the NPCI per-transaction limit in rupees; it drives a NON-BLOCKING warning only, never a hard stop. The `capInr` on the `lite` spend codes (44/45) is ALSO the UPI Lite per-payment limit the app uses to decide when to offer the UPI / UPI Lite choice for a payment — raise it here when NPCI does.",
